{
  "concept": "The tangent line to a curve at a point P is the limiting position of the secant lines through P and a nearby point Q as Q slides along the curve toward P.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Panel (a): x-axis and y-axis with arrowheads, labeled 'x' and 'y', drawn in black",
    "Panel (a): a smooth blue open curve rising from lower-left, cresting, and falling to the right (a hump/cubic-like shape)",
    "Fixed blue point P on the left flank of the curve, labeled 'P' in italic",
    "Movable blue point Q on the curve to the right of P, labeled 'Q' in italic",
    "Family of pink/magenta secant lines through P and successive Q positions, fanning out",
    "Limiting pink tangent line at P, drawn slightly thicker/darker",
    "Shaded pink-to-white gradient wedge between the steepest secant and the tangent line, showing the swept region",
    "Curved gray arrow with open arrowhead sweeping from the shallowest secant toward the tangent line, indicating direction of the limit",
    "Text label 'Tangent line' near the top-left of the fan",
    "Text label 'Secant line' at the right end of the shallowest secant",
    "Panel (b): a blue circle with the same construction — fixed P on the upper-left of the circle, movable Q on the upper-right",
    "Panel (b): fan of pink secant lines through P and Q, limiting pink tangent line touching the circle at P, shaded wedge, curved gray arrow",
    "Panel (b) labels 'P', 'Q', 'Tangent line', 'Secant line'",
    "Panel captions '(a)' and '(b)' centered below each diagram",
    "Live readout of secant slope m_PQ and limiting tangent slope, plus the distance Q→P",
    "Faint ghost traces of previously drawn secant lines (the fan)"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "panel",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Curve",
      "teaches": "The same limiting construction defines the tangent on an arbitrary smooth curve and reproduces the familiar 'touches at one point' tangent on a circle.",
      "options": ["(a) smooth curve", "(b) circle"],
      "default": "(a) smooth curve"
    },
    {
      "id": "qPosition",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Position of Q along the curve (arc distance from P)",
      "teaches": "As Q approaches P the secant line pivots continuously and its slope converges to a single limiting value — the tangent slope.",
      "range": [0.02, 1.0, 0.01],
      "default": 1.0
    },
    {
      "id": "pPosition",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Position of P along the curve",
      "teaches": "The tangent line is local: moving P changes the limiting direction, so the tangent slope is a function of position, not a property of the whole curve.",
      "range": [0.0, 1.0, 0.01],
      "default": 0.2
    },
    {
      "id": "showFan",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Show secant fan (ghost traces)",
      "teaches": "Seeing many secants at once makes the convergence visible as a fan collapsing onto one limiting line, exactly as in the printed figure.",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "A far-away secant",
      "narration": "Q sits well to the right of P on the blue curve; the pink line through P and Q is a secant, cutting the curve at two clearly separate points. Its slope is the average rate of change between P and Q.",
      "state": { "panel": "(a) smooth curve", "qPosition": 1.0, "pPosition": 0.2, "showFan": false }
    },
    {
      "title": "Sliding Q toward P",
      "narration": "Drag Q closer to P and the secant pivots about P, steepening as the slope readout climbs. Each intermediate position leaves a ghost secant, building the pink fan.",
      "state": { "panel": "(a) smooth curve", "qPosition": 0.45, "pPosition": 0.2, "showFan": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "The limiting position",
      "narration": "With Q almost on top of P the secants have collapsed onto one line — the tangent. The slope readout has settled on a definite limiting value even though Q never actually reaches P.",
      "state": { "panel": "(a) smooth curve", "qPosition": 0.03, "pPosition": 0.2, "showFan": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "The tangent is local",
      "narration": "Move P to the crest of the curve and repeat: the limiting line is now horizontal. The tangent direction depends on where on the curve you stand.",
      "state": { "panel": "(a) smooth curve", "qPosition": 0.05, "pPosition": 0.55, "showFan": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Does it match the circle?",
      "narration": "Switch to the circle and run the same construction. The limiting line touches the circle at P only and is perpendicular to the radius — the new definition agrees with the classical geometric tangent.",
      "state": { "panel": "(b) circle", "qPosition": 0.04, "pPosition": 0.35, "showFan": true }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The tangent line is not defined by 'touching at one point' — it is the line the secants are heading toward; the slope has a limit even though the secant through P and Q never exists when Q = P.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two side-by-side panels sharing a white background. Left panel (a): black x- and y-axes with arrowheads and italic labels; a thick blue (#2196c4) smooth curve rising from lower-left, peaking right of center, then falling. Blue filled dots mark P (on the rising left flank) and Q (farther right, on the shallow descent). Three to four magenta/plum (#a0459b) straight secant lines all pass through P at increasing steepness; the steepest is the tangent. A soft pink gradient wedge fills the angular region between the steepest secant and the tangent, fading to white outward. A thin light-gray curved arrow with an open, outlined arrowhead sweeps counterclockwise from the shallowest secant up to the tangent. 'Tangent line' labels the upper-left ray; 'Secant line' labels the right end of the shallowest ray. Right panel (b): same palette, a blue circle of moderate radius with P on the upper-left rim and Q on the upper-right rim; the same fan of magenta secants through P, limiting tangent grazing the circle at P, shaded wedge and gray sweep arrow, with 'Tangent line' upper-left and 'Secant line' at the right. Italic '(a)' and '(b)' centered beneath each panel. Add a small unobtrusive readout box showing m_secant, m_tangent, and Q−P separation; lines being ghosted should be drawn thin and semi-transparent in the same magenta."
}

